# Git identity — webmaster-dfc (STRICT)

All commits pushed to **github.com/webmaster-dfc/** must use:

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| **user.name** | `webmaster-dfc` |
| **user.email** | `webmaster@drugfreecompliance.com` |

## Repos (each is its own git root)

- `~/mac/slark/dfc/dfc-backend` → `webmaster-dfc/dfc-backend`
- `~/mac/slark/dfc/dfc-frontend` → `webmaster-dfc/dfc-frontend`
- `~/mac/slark/dfc/dfc-admin` → `webmaster-dfc/dfc-admin`

## Before every commit (agent MUST)

1. **Never** commit as `Ammar Chaudhry`, `mac@…local`, Cursor default, `macbuilds-dev`, or `muhammadammarchaudhry1@gmail.com`.
2. Use **`--author`** on every commit (do not rely on auto-detected hostname identity):

```bash
git commit --author="webmaster-dfc <webmaster@drugfreecompliance.com>" -m "…"
```

3. Optional one-time **local** config per repo (not global):

```bash
cd ~/mac/slark/dfc/dfc-backend   # repeat for frontend + admin
git config user.name "webmaster-dfc"
git config user.email "webmaster@drugfreecompliance.com"
```

4. Verify before push:

```bash
git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>'
# must show: webmaster-dfc <webmaster@drugfreecompliance.com>
```

## Push target

- **Remote:** `origin` → `https://github.com/webmaster-dfc/<repo>.git`
- **Branch:** `main` unless user specifies otherwise
- **Never** force-push `main` unless user explicitly asks
